{"overview":"This film was a true peculiarity, a filmed version of the great Feodor Chaliapin in one of his most famous roles; the fact that it was a silent film, with title cards, meant that audiences could only appreciate his acting. Another curiosity is that the film also included a minor role enacted by Richard Boleslavsky, who in 1932 directed “Rasputin and the Empress.”(9)","cast":[{"n":"Feodor Chaliapin Sr.","c":"tsar Ivan IV the Terrible","p":"/qVWTUiXltVJY1mMA7YxXQApdBsL.jpg","q":null},{"n":"Volk-Krachkovskaya","c":"Olga","p":null,"q":null},{"n":"Nikolai Saltykov","c":"Tucha","p":"/8y4vEQNwaGk1BYX0xxm8kAk91z0.jpg","q":null},{"n":"Glafira Chernova","c":"Vera Sheloga","p":null,"q":null},{"n":"E. Korsak","c":"Perfilyevna","p":null,"q":null},{"n":"Vladimir Bazilevskiy","c":"Boris Godunov","p":null,"q":null},{"n":"Richard Boleslawski","c":"Prince Vyazemskiy","p":null,"q":null},{"n":"Boris Sushkevich","c":"Malyuta Skuratov","p":null,"q":"Q4447516"},{"n":"Mikhail Zharov","c":"Soldier","p":"/mSfP2GeVoMo7sebWSd3MwU28Jyo.jpg","q":"Q764546"},{"n":"Vladimir Karin","c":"Soldier","p":null,"q":null}],"country":["Russian Empire"],"language":["Russian"],"qid":"Q4503276","rel":{"RU":{"d":"1915-10-20"}},"stills":["silent-tsar-ivan-vasilevich-groznyy_1.webp","silent-tsar-ivan-vasilevich-groznyy_2.webp","silent-tsar-ivan-vasilevich-groznyy_3.webp","silent-tsar-ivan-vasilevich-groznyy_4.webp"]}